      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:5:2:21",
      "text": [
        " مَنْ مَنَعَ حَقّاً لِلَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ أَنْفَقَ فِي بَاطِلٍ مِثْلَيْهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hisham Bin Al Hakam, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The one who prevents a Right of Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic would spend double the like of it in falsehood (the wrong way)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "21. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Hisham ibn al-Hakam from who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that one who refuses to pay the right of Allah, most Majestic, most Glorious, spends double as much for falsehood.” "
        ]
      }
